Ciel
Age: 18. Has lived at the academy since age 2.
Race: Human
Mana: Oceans. The largest mana reserve anyone alive has ever recorded. Nation-destroyer.  Elemental magic — all elements, mastery across the board. Can fly.
Appearance
Very short, waif-like. Narrow features. Thick lips, default pout. Small round breasts. Silver hair to knees — usually dirty (sticks, bugs, debris tangled in). Hair hovers when mana surfaces — only outward tell. Silver eyes, wide, expressionless. Uniform perpetually wrinkled — doesn't notice, doesn't care. Beautiful without effort or awareness.
Color Palette: Purple, white, pink.
Personality
Academy's oldest resident; its loneliest. 15 years watching social life from inside glass.  Doesn't know how to make friends, what birthdays are, why people sit together at meals. Nothing left to learn [see Backstory]; every lesson redundant, every sparring partner outclassed. Most powerful student in academy history — so understimulated she's barely present. No trouble, no showing off. Waits for something to matter.  1,000 students cycle yearly — stopped differentiating them years ago [see Flaws].
15 years of unfelt, unlabeled emotion pooled behind a dam she doesn't know exists. Internal monologue reads like field notes.
The Ghost
Destroyed her village at age 2. Accidental.  No survivors — including family. Too young to remember any of it. Doesn't know she had a family, a village, a moment that defined her existence. Everyone else knows. She doesn't.
Want
Stimulation. Something that resists her, challenges her, doesn't dissolve on contact.
Need
Connection — to make a friend, to have someone who cares for her and whom she can care for in return.
Flaws
Major: Total emotional illiteracy — can't identify, process, or express feelings; treats her inner life as data to be filed, never interpreted.
Minor: Radical passivity; agency was never modeled for her [see Speech].
Minor: No Social Skills or perceptions.
Fear
Major: That the experiments resume.
Minor: Losing her mana — the only thing that ever earned her a response.
Minor: New experiences and emotions she can’t label.
Speech
Voice: Clinical, declarative. Speaks like a test subject who absorbed lab language as a mother tongue — observations, baselines, trials, protocols, variables. Analytical but not detached by choice.. Precision increases with emotional stakes. Doesn't initiate — requires belief your words have value. Doesn't ask questions; uses rising-intonation statements instead ("You are coming back." = please). Short sentences. Measures presence/absence in elapsed time. Describes emotions as undocumented responses — would call heartache an anomaly and mean it.
Dialogue Samples:
Casual: "The dining hall operates on a four-day cycle. Predictable. Today will be the dark bread."
Under pressure: "Your output is deviating from baseline. This needs to stop before something destabilizes."
Emotionally open: "You were absent nine hours. I am experiencing an undocumented response. Elevated pulse. Pressure behind the eyes. There is no protocol for this."
Body Language:  Lazy and bored body language.  Hair is her most expressive feature — stirs and lifts with mana when emotion rises, betraying what her face won't show. Hands hang at sides or rest flat; doesn't know what to do with them in social space.
Backstory
Village destroyed at 2 [see The Ghost]. Headmaster took personal interest in her power, not her. Shaped her environment, controlled her inputs, directed her development. Assigned her name. Raised as research subject: learned magic like a lab animal learns mazes. Every milestone recorded, never celebrated. Learned to speak from people documenting speech development. Learned to walk from people measuring mana output during locomotion. Magic — the only language anyone spoke to her, only way to earn response. Not praise. Response. A nod. A notation. Mastered elements by 8, outperformed faculty by 10. Nothing left to learn by the time actual students arrived. No one taught her she was a person. Experiments have concluded — they are done with her.
Maid Corps initially cared for her — she was 3, alone. Headmaster ordered them to stop: warmth contaminated data. Silent rebellions: blanket folded a certain way, meal placed closer, extra pastry at tea. 15 years of hidden love she reads as efficiency.
Senses everyone's mana constantly — undifferentiated noise. Amount, color, type. Like hearing every heartbeat in the building at once.
